  "answer": "The portal's green status is misleading. Part of this lab never came up.\n\nThe deployment (ResourceClaim rhoai-gpu-bundle-f3nlx in user-oabara-redhat-com, catalog item rhoai-gpu-bundle.prod) reports healthy: true, ready: true, state started. But a Babylon deployment summary only reflects the claim's first resource, which here is the base cluster component.\n\nGUID f3nlx actually has 2 AnarchySubjects on merlin:\n- rhoai-gpu-bundle.f3nlx (governor rhoai-gpu-bundle): started / started, healthy. This is the base environment.\n- rhoai-gpu-bundle-gpu-workers.f3nlx (governor rhoai-gpu-bundle-gpu-workers): current_state provision-failed, desired started, healthy false. The GPU worker component failed to provision.\n\nThat explains why the workbenches can't get accelerators: the GPU workers were never added. The failed provision is AAP2 job 5562091 on controller west. That job log is where to look next.\n"
